+# Baileys 7 migration changes
+
+This Termux build targets `@whiskeysockets/baileys` `^7.0.0-rc13` on Node.js 20 or newer.
+
+Implemented changes:
+
+- Loads the ESM-only Baileys package from the existing CommonJS bot through dynamic `import()`.
+- Replaces removed protobuf `.fromObject()` calls with `.create()`.
+- Replaces the removed built-in memory store with a small event-backed message/contact store.
+- Uses `useMultiFileAuthState`, pairing-code login, QR fallback, credential updates and reconnect handling.
+- Handles Baileys 7 LID/PN alternate fields for owner and group-admin checks.
+- Removes the original embedded WhatsApp session, public MongoDB passwords and hard-coded developer-owner number.
+- Removes the unused `wa-sticker-formatter` dependency that pulled native `sharp` builds on Termux.
+- Repairs corrupted plugin-manager/updater files and prevents the updater from overwriting this migration.
+- Initializes local JSON state correctly and uses one database-save timer instead of creating one per message.
+
+Validation performed:
+
+- All JavaScript source files pass `node --check` through `npm run check`.
+- Project JSON files parse successfully.
+- No old Baileys fork imports, `makeInMemoryStore`, or protobuf `.fromObject()` calls remain.
+
+A complete dependency installation was not executed in the build sandbox because registry resolution timed out. Run `bash termux-setup.sh` in Termux to install the dependencies on the target device.
