+# Termux deployment — Baileys 7 RC13
+
+Keep the project in Termux home (`$HOME`), not directly in shared Android storage. Android shared storage can break npm links and executable permissions.
+
+## 1. Extract into Termux home
+
+```bash
+termux-setup-storage
+pkg update -y
+pkg install -y unzip
+cd "$HOME"
+rm -rf KING-VAJIRA-MD-Baileys7-Termux
+unzip "$HOME/storage/downloads/KING-VAJIRA-MD-Baileys7-Termux.zip"
+cd KING-VAJIRA-MD-Baileys7-Termux
+```
+
+## 2. Install and configure
+
+```bash
+bash termux-setup.sh
+nano config.env
+```
+
+Set these two values in `config.env` using international format without `+`, spaces, or dashes:
+
+```env
+PAIRING_NUMBER=2637XXXXXXXX
+OWNER_NUMBER=2637XXXXXXXX
+```
+
+MongoDB is optional for startup, but database-backed commands need your own `MONGODB_URI`.
+
+## 3. Start and pair
+
+```bash
+npm run check
+npm start
+```
+
+The terminal prints a pairing code. In WhatsApp, open **Linked devices → Link a device → Link with phone number**, then enter the code.
+
+## Keep it running
+
+After pairing, stop the foreground process with `Ctrl+C`, then run:
+
+```bash
+termux-wake-lock
+npm run start:pm2
+npx pm2 save
+```
+
+Useful commands:
+
+```bash
+npx pm2 logs king-vajira-md
+npx pm2 restart king-vajira-md
+npx pm2 stop king-vajira-md
+```
+
+Authentication is stored in `lib/auth_info_baileys/`. Keep that directory private and back it up before replacing the project.
